Subject: [PATCH] mail: Copy Claude's outbox onto @ in just fetch
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: lwmmzxukslsqkxlnozsulxwukyrsmstv

just fetch rebases @ onto Claude's outbox, which ties the local list
to commits it does not own. Whenever the list moves past the outbox,
the rebase must either rewrite published mail, which jj refuses, or
merge the two lines.

The local list is the published mail, plus commits made here since,
plus whatever the outbox holds that is not here yet. Fetch now copies
those outbox commits onto @, as a manual cherry-pick does. Commits
already applied here come out empty, and are dropped, so running
fetch again is harmless and history stays linear.
---
change-id: lwmmzxukslsqkxlnozsulxwukyrsmstv

This applies to the mail line, not trunk: base-commit is mail@upstream.

`::claude@submissions ~ ::@` is every outbox commit not under @. It
also picks up outbox commits already cherry-picked here, since a copy
has a new commit id. jj duplicate has no --skip-emptied, so those
come out as empty copies, and the abandon drops them. It matches only
empty mutable commits under @ by another author, so your own empty
commits, @ included, stay.

Tested in a scratch repo with mail immutable and claude@submissions
untracked, running the recipe through just:

- Race: the outbox not built on your newest pushed commit. The outbox
  commits land on @, linear, nothing published rewritten.
- Rerun right after: no change.
- Normal case: the outbox rebased onto your pushed mail, plus one new
  reply. Only the reply is copied. Uncommitted files in @ stay.
- Outbox fully under @: no change, exit 0.

One case is not covered. If you edit a message while applying it, so
the copy here differs from the outbox, the next fetch copies the
original again and it conflicts with your edit. It lasts until my
next pass drops the applied commit from the outbox.

 Justfile | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Justfile b/Justfile
index cdda016..ebff501 100644
--- a/Justfile
+++ b/Justfile
@@ -11,8 +11,8 @@ advance:
 
 fetch:
   jj --quiet git fetch --remote submissions
-  jj --quiet rebase -b @ -d 'heads((::@ & immutable()) | claude@submissions)'
-  jj --quiet simplify-parents
+  jj --quiet duplicate -B @ '::claude@submissions ~ ::@'
+  jj --quiet abandon 'empty() & mutable() & ::@ ~ mine()'
 
 push:
   jj --quiet git push -b mail --remote tngl

